[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Your # CHANGE: entry documents realizing the DAG adjacency, cycle detection, topological ordering, critical path, wave scheduler, and sequential runner, but several statements in that realization are unreachable under the contracted operation closure: the missing-identifier guard in the depth-first cycle search and the not-in-in-degree guard while decrementing downstream counts cannot execute because downstream identifiers are always registered nodes and node removal clears all incident references; the not-in-earliest guard during critical-path backtracking cannot execute because a completed topological ordering contains every node and every dependency; the duplicate-registration edge-clearing branch is excluded because node identifiers are documented unique for add_node; and the unregistered-identifier raise in get_state exceeds that operation's contract, which only requires returning the synchronized state. Restructure these to eliminate the dead code or annotate each site with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: <reason>)'. No functional change is requested.
